ite paint £4.99 tiles £19.99 doorbell electrics 15.99 grass seed £1.99 matt white paint decorating 4.99 -£0.20 discount lawn mower £129.99 tiles decorating 19.99 -£13.00 discount ---------------- grass seed gardening 1.99 total: £198.89 lawn mower gardening 129.99 fig. 2 fig. 3 write an algorithm in pseudocode, using the array purchases, to: • determine which items are given a discount • calculate the total price to pay • present this information on a receipt in the format shown in fig. 3. [6] question answer marks guidance 7 6 example  prints receipt with item name and price on each line. (ao3.2) decoratingspend = 0.0  applies a 10% discount to gardening purchases. for i = 0 to purchases[].size() (ao3.2) if purchases[i,1] == ”decorating” then a02.1  if decorating spend is £20 or more. (ao3.2) decoratingspend = decoratingspend + (1) float(purchases[i,2])  displays each discount on the receipt. (ao3.2) ao3.2 endif  displays the correct total. (ao3.2) (5) next i  correct addressing of a 2d array (a02.1) total = 0.0 disc = 0.0 for i = 0 to purchases[].size() print(purchases[i,0] + ” £” + purchases[i,2]) total = total + float(purchases[i,2]) if decoratingspend >= 20 and purchases[i,1] == ”gardening” then disc = round(float(purchases[i,2]) * 0.1, 2) print(“-£” + str(disc) + ” d","h04601-jun17-01-ai":"1 (a) processors following the von neumann architecture use registers. (i) describe what is meant by the term ‘register’. [2] question assessment objectives total ao1.1 ao1.2 ao2.1 ao2.2 ao3.1 ao3.2 ao3.3 1ai 2 0 0 0 0 0 0 2","h04601-jun17-01-aii":"1 (a) processors following the von neumann architecture use registers. (ii) give one other feature of the von neumann architecture. [1] 1aii 1 0 0 0 0 0 0 1","h04601-jun17-01-b":"(b) an example of a register is the accumulator (acc). give a little man computer instruction that will copy the contents of the accumulator into memory when executed. [1] (b) -sta 1 accept sto ao1.2","h04601-jun17-01-ci":"(c) another register is th