accept answer without brackets. ao2.2 accept alternative notation i.e. or , + a ∨ b (1 mark) ∨ (c ∨ d) (1 mark)","h04601-jun17-07-a":"7 a company releases an internet connected fridge. users can email messages to the fridge and it puts them on its display. (a) the fridge uses the tcp/ip stack. explain what is meant by the term ‘tcp/ip stack’. [3] 7 (a) - stands for “transmission control protocol / 1 accept layers in any order. internet protocol”… (1) ao1.1 accept data link instead of link. - protocol(s)/set of rules… (1) 2 ignore any mention of physical layer. - …for communicating across a network / the a01.2 do not accept network for internet layer. internet. (1) mp3 is dependent on either mp1 or mp2 being awarded. - each protocol belongs to a different layer. (1) - the layers are: application, transport, internet, link (1) - (starting at the application layer) data is further encapsulated as it as it is passed to the next layer. (1)","h04601-jun17-07-b":"7 a company releases an internet connected fridge. users can email messages to the fridge and it puts them on its display. (b) the fridge uses the ascii character set. give one disadvantage of the fridge using ascii rather than unicode. [1] when the fridge receives a message it takes the string and stores it in a queue called words. for example remember to take charlie to the dentist this afternoon becomes a queue: words=[\"remember\",\"to\",\"take\",\"charlie\",\"to\",\"the\",\"dentist\", \"this\",\"afternoon\"] words.remove() then returns the next item in the queue for example temp=words.remove() assigns temp the value \"remember\" and leaves words as [\"to\",\"take\",\"charlie\",\"to\",\"the\",\"dentist\",\"this\",\"afternoon\"] the display has four lines; each can show a maximum of 20 characters including spaces. if a word can’t fit on a line a new line is started. examples r e m e m b e r t o t a k e c h a r l i e t o t h e d e n t i s t t h i s a f t e r n o o n g e t s o m e m o r e c h o c o l a t e p l e a s e the contents of the display are stored in a 2d array of characters called display. the procedure updatedisplay receives the queue words which holds the message and writes the message to the display. (b) - fewer characters can be represented (1) 1 accept: special symbols, such as emoticons, can’t be represented. ao1.2 - characters from different languages can’t be represented. (1)","h04601-jun17-07-c":"7 a company releases an internet connected fridge. users can email messages to the fridge and it puts them on its display. (c) write the procedure updatedisplay. credit will be given for the readability of your code. you can assume: • messages contain no punctuation. • all messages will fit on the display. • the previous message is removed before the procedure is run. global array display[20,4] … … … procedure updatedisplay(words) endprocedure [7] (c) - program iterates through the queue words (1) 7 global array display[20,4] ao3.2 - first word is added to display (1) … (5) - subsequent words added on the same line (1) procedure updatedisplay(words[]) ao3.1 xpos=0 - unless a word won’t fit, in which case it is moved to the next line (1) (2) ypos=0 - words have spaces between them. (1) for i=0 to words.size-1 temp=words.remove() - use of sensible variable names (allow single letter if xpos+1+temp.length>20 then variables for for loop counters. (1) ypos=ypos+1 - use of indentation (1) xpos=0 endif for j=0 to temp.length-1 display[xpos+j, ypos]=temp.substring(j,1) next j xpos=xpos+temp.length+1 next i endprocedure accept ‘row major’ array in pseudocode provided it is consistent throughout.","h04601-jun17-08":"8* many websites try to ensure they are accessible to all visitors regardless of disability, language spoken or the device being used to access it. discuss the technical and design measures that can be taken to ensure a website is accessible. [9] 8 mark band 3–high level 9 ao1: knowledge and understanding (7-9 marks) the candidate demonstrates a thorough knowle