ll of the separate video elements together to form the final video. (a) describe two factors that affect the performance of the cpu. 1 2 [4] question answer mark guidance 1 (a) • ao1.1 one mark for stating the factor, mark for expanding the clock speed … • (2) factor … the speed at which the fetch decode execute ao1.2 cycle is completed/ the speed a single core can (2) - accept cycles for “fde cycles” execute instructions • number of cores/ independent processing units … • …that can fetch decode execute at the same time • cache size… • … memory that contains recently/frequently used instructions/data • …memory that has a faster r/w speed than ram • …memory that is closer to/onboard the cpu","h04601-jun23-01-b":"1 ocrsystems are designing a new cpu for a computer system that will be used for video rendering. part of the video rendering process is when the video is exported. this is when the computer combines all of the separate video elements together to form the final video. (b) an important design consideration is whether ocrsystems use a cisc processor type or a risc processor type. describe one difference between a cisc processor and a risc processor. [2] 1 (b) • ao1.2 accept any other valid points cisc has a larger instruction set • (2) risc has a smaller instruction set mark in pairs • cisc is difficult to pipeline • risc is easier to pipeline • cisc tends to have more addressing modes • risc tends to have fewer addressing modes • cisc instructions may take multiple clock cycles to execute • risc instructions take one clock cycle to execute • cisc has complex circuitry/more transistors. • risc has less complex/simple circuitry • cisc uses less ram • risc uses more ram","h04601-jun23-01-c":"1 ocrsystems are designing a new cpu for a computer system that will be used for video rendering. part of the video rendering process is when the video is exported. this is when the computer combines all of the separate video elements together to form the final video. (c) ocr