ing date in date of birth additional guidance: • outputting age, day, month and year in message only penalise type casting in bp2. ft thereafter in all • …that matches example format with suitable calculations. concatenation. candidates are not provided with ‘syntax’ ","h04602-jun25-08":"8 show each pass of a bubble sort to sort the following string data into descending order. friend sun earth orange night time [4] 8 1 mark for first pass resulting in: 4 if ascending order, mark as ft and max 3: • sun friend orange night time earth pass 1: f e o n s t 1 mark for second pass resulting in: • pass 2: e f n o s t sun orange night time friend earth pass 3: e f n o s t if ascending, third mark is for 1 mark for 3rd, pass resulting in: showing pass 3 has no swaps and therefore the list is • 3rd sun orange time night friend earth sorted. 1 mark for 4th and 5th passes resulting in: • 4th sun time orange night friend earth • 5th time sun orange night friend earth","h04602-nov20-01-ai":"1 sally is a classroom teacher. she would like a program to be able to organise where students will sit in her classroom. a plan of her classroom is shown in fig. 1. storage units zingzing susan banks matthew alter foggin rob harry naheed shah anderson jefferies demmi alex oldman rashida cunningham ali teacher desk door white board fig. 1 (a) (i) state three ways that sally has made use of abstraction in fig. 1. 1 2 3 [3] question answer mark guidance 1 (a) (i) 1 mark per bullet up to a maximum of 3 marks, e.g: 3 allow other suitable responses that are applied to the scenario in the question. • classroom displays have been removed a02.1 • people have been removed / simplified with (3) symbols • wall/carpet colours/details have been removed • diagram is not to scale.","h04602-nov20-01-aii":"1 sally is a classroom teacher. she would like a program to be able to organise where students will sit in her classroom. a plan of her classroom is shown in fig. 1. storage units zingzing susan banks matthew