h a red light. input green light red light 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8 9 \b [2] 1bi 2 2","h44601-jun18-01-bii":"(b) part of the coffee making machine’s code asks the user to press a button to select strength. the code outputs 1 which will switch on a green light to indicate a valid selection or outputs 0 to indicate an invalid selection. the code is shown below: inp sta entry lda max sub entry brp accept lda redlight bra printandend accept lda greenlight printandend out hlt greenlight dat 1 redlight dat 0 max dat 5 entry dat fig. 1 1 a digital coffee making machine has a cpu that uses the little man computer instruction set. (ii) explain which registers and buses are used, and the values they store/carry, when the line lda redlight is executed (after it has been fetched and decoded). you should assume the address redlight refers to memory location 11. \b������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������� [6] 1bii 6 6","h44601-jun18-01-biii":"(b) part of the coffee making machine’s code asks the user to press a button to select strength. the code outputs 1 which will switch on a green light to indicate a valid selection or outputs 0 to indicate an invalid selection. the code is shown below: inp sta entry lda max sub entry brp accept lda redlight bra printandend accept lda greenlight printandend out hlt greenlight dat 1 redlight dat 0 max dat 5 entry dat fig. 1 1 a digital coffee making machine has a cpu that uses the little man computer instruction set. (iii) write code in a high‑level language or pseudocode that has the same functionality as the code in fig. 1. \b������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������� [3] 1biii 3 3","h44601-jun18-01-biv":"(b) part of the coffee making machine’s code asks the user to press a button to select strength. the code outputs 1 which will switch on a green light to in