riented programming. the design for the class, its attributes and methods are shown: class: stack attributes: private stackarray : array of integer private pointervalue : integer methods: new() function pop() function push(value) 8 a computer uses a stack data structure, implemented using an array, to store numbers entered by the user. the array is zero based and has 100 locations. (iii) the main program initialises a new object of type stack with the identifier mathsstack. write pseudocode or program code to declare the object. [2] 1 mark per bullet 2 accept mathsstack = stack() • instantiation of new object of type stack • assigned to variable mathsstack 8biii allow missing brackets this time only e.g. mathsstack = stack mathsstack = new stack()","h44602-jun22-08-biv":"(b) the stack is programmed as an object using object-oriented programming. the design for the class, its attributes and methods are shown: class: stack attributes: private stackarray : array of integer private pointervalue : integer methods: new() function pop() function push(value) 8 a computer uses a stack data structure, implemented using an array, to store numbers entered by the user. the array is zero based and has 100 locations. (iv) the main program needs to: • take numbers as input from the user • push them onto the stack mathsstack until the stack is full • output an appropriate message if the stack is full. complete the pseudocode algorithm to meet these requirements. returnvalue = true while returnvalue == returnvalue = mathsstack. (input(\"enter number\")) if returnvalue == then (\"stack full\") endif endwhile [4] 1 mark for each completed statement 4 accept equivalent for print e.g. output returnvalue = true while returnvalue == true returnvalue = mathsstack.push(input(\"enter number\")) 8biv if returnvalue == false then print(\"stack full\") endif","h44602-jun22-08-bv":"(b) the stack is programmed as an object using object-oriented programming. the design for the class, its attributes and methods are shown: class: stack attributes: private stackarray : array of integer private pointervalue : integer methods: new() function pop() function push(value) 8 a computer uses a stack data structure, implemented using an array, to store numbers entered by the user. the array is zero based and has 100 locations. (v) the main program also needs to: • remove one item from the stack at a time and add this to a total • output the total every time an item is removed • stop removing items when either the stack is empty, or 20 items have been removed. write pseudocode or program code to meet these requirements. 1 mark per bullet to max 8 8 • initialise a total to 0 outside of loop • looping • removing an item from the stack using the method pop • check if stack is empty • (if not) add value returned to total • …outputting total • counting how many values are returned • stopping loop when either 20 items removed or no items left total = 0 quantity = 0 8bv returnvalue = 0 while quantity<20 and retunvalue!=-1 returnvalue = mathsstack.pop() if(returnvalue != -1) then quantity = quantity + 1 total = total + returnvalue print(total) endif endwhile","h44602-jun22-08-ci":"8 a computer uses a stack data structure, implemented using an array, to store numbers entered by the user. the array is zero based and has 100 locations. (c) the program is amended to include the use of several queue data structures. (i) describe how an array can be used to implement a queue data structure. [3] 1 mark per bullet to max 3 max 1 mark for enqueue/dequeue operations if description of effect on • queue has head pointer and tail pointer 8ci tail/head pointers not given • when an item is enqueued the tail pointer increments • when an item is dequeued the head pointer increments","h44602-jun22-08-cii":"(c) the program is amended to include the use of several queue data structures. 8 a computer uses a stack data structure, implemented using an array, to store numbers entered by the user. the ar