und) ………………………………) if upperbound < lowerbound then return …………………………………………… else if dataarray[middle] < searchvalue then lowerbound = ……………………………………………………………………………………………………………………… elseif dataarray[middle] > searchvalue then upperbound = ……………………………………………………………………………………………………………………… else return …………………………………………………………………………………………… endif endif endwhile endfunction [6] 1 mark for each number/statement up to a maximum of 6 marks: function binarysearch(dataarray:byref, upperbound, lowerbound, searchvalue) while true middle = lowerbound + ((upperbound - lowerbound) div 2) if upperbound < lowerbound then return -1 else 6 if dataarray[middle] < searchvalue then ao1.2 2ai lowerbound = middle + 1 (2) ao3.3 (4) elseif dataarray[middle] > searchvalue then upperbound = middle - 1 else return middle endif endif endwhile endfunction","h44602-nov21-02-aii":"(a) the pseudocode binary search algorithm is incomplete. 2 the pseudocode function binarysearch() performs a binary search on the array dataarray that is passed as a parameter. the function returns the array index of searchvalue within the array, and -1 if it is not in the array. (ii) the algorithm uses a while loop. state a different type of loop that could be used instead of the while loop in the given algorithm. [1] 1 2aii do…until // repeat…until // post condition ao1.2 (1)","h44602-nov21-02-b":"2 the pseudocode function binarysearch() performs a binary search on the array dataarray that is passed as a parameter. the function returns the array index of searchvalue within the array, and -1 if it is not in the array. (b) the tables below show possible big o complexities for the worst-case space, best-case space and average time for search algorithms. tick the worst-case space complexity for a binary and linear search. binary linear search search o(log(n)) o(1) o(n) tick the best-case space complexity for a binary and linear search. binary linear search search o(log(n)) o(1) o(n) tick the average time complexity for a binary an