ce memory requirements (1)","h04602-jun18-03-aiii":"3 a country’s national rail operator wants to represent their rail network on a computer system to keep track of the location of trains, and any problems on the network. after studying the rail network, the operator uses abstraction to create the virtual representation. (iii) describe one potential difference between the virtual and real rail network. [2] 3 (a) (iii) 1 mark per identifying difference, 1 for expansion 2 ao2.1 e.g. (1)  removal of feature ao2.2  e.g. no stations/signals (1)  symbols/keys are used to represent elements  e.g. the train  may not be to scale  relative distances may not be true","h04602-jun18-03-bi":"3 a country’s national rail operator wants to represent their rail network on a computer system to keep track of the location of trains, and any problems on the network. after studying the rail network, the operator uses abstraction to create the virtual representation. (b) the rail operator provides an app for customers to purchase tickets. an array is used to store the names of the stations on the network. customers must enter a departure station into the app. the current contents of the array are shown: council cavalry bridge walkway museum monument theatre cinema house a linear search is used to check if the entered departure station exists in the array. (i) identify one precondition that is needed before a binary search could be used with the station array. [1] 3 (b) (i) the data needs to be sorted / in alphabetical order 1 ao2.1 (1)","h04602-jun18-03-bii":"(b) the rail operator provides an app for customers to purchase tickets. an array is used to store the names of the stations on the network. customers must enter a departure station into the app. the current contents of the array are shown: council cavalry bridge walkway museum monument theatre cinema house a linear search is used to check if the entered departure station exists in the array. 3 a country’s national rail operator