ptr <= rightptr) midpoint = (leftptr + rightptr) div 2 if (numberarray[midpoint] == targetnum","h04602-jun16-04-ci":"(c) the target integer 8 exists in a list of integers 1, 4, 6, 9, 8, 12, 15 but is not found during a binary search. there are no errors in the code. (i) give the reason why the target integer 8 is not found. [1] question answer/indicative content mark guidance 1 (c) i  the integers in the list are unsorted (1) ao2.1 (1) ii identification (max 1) 3 accept serial ao1.1  perform a linear search description (max 2)  starting at the first element / each item is checked…  until value is found  or end of list reached and not found","h04602-jun16-04-cii":"(c) the target integer 8 exists in a list of integers 1, 4, 6, 9, 8, 12, 15 but is not found during a binary search. there are no errors in the code. (ii) identify and describe an alternative search algorithm that could be used. [3] question answer/indicative content mark guidance 1 (c) i  the integers in the list are unsorted (1) ao2.1 (1) ii identification (max 1) 3 accept serial ao1.1  perform a linear search description (max 2)  starting at the first element / each item is checked…  until value is found  or end of list reached and not found","h04602-jun16-04-d":"(d) a stack, in shared memory, is being used to pass a single variable length ascii string between two sub-systems. the string is placed in the stack one character at a time in reverse order with the last byte holding the number of characters pushed i.e the text “silver” would be held in the stack as: 6 top s i l v e r use pseudocode to write a procedure that will take a text string passed to it and push it to the stack in the format defined above. you may assume any given input will fit in the stack. [6] question answer/indicative content mark guidance 6 (d)  string length calculated (1) allow stackptr to be used instead of i in loop, as we ao3.2 would not expect them to know that some compilers do not  correct number of characters 