) or (b >= c)) then if ((c < a ) xor (c < b)) then // check to see if one or the other // comparisons are true, but not both d = 15 else d = 16 endif else d = 14 endif print(d) (c) state the value of d if a=42, b=36 and c=36 4 7 (a)  16 max 4 marks ao2.2 b  16 (4) c  15 d  42  43 (max. 1)","h04602-jun16-07-d":"7 given the following pseudocode: d = 5 if ((a > b) or (b >= c)) then if ((c < a ) xor (c < b)) then // check to see if one or the other // comparisons are true, but not both d = 15 else d = 16 endif else d = 14 endif print(d) (d) give one potential value of b if the output value of a=42, c=44 and d=14. [4] 4 7 (a)  16 max 4 marks ao2.2 b  16 (4) c  15 d  42  43 (max. 1)","h44601-nov20-01-ai":"1 a hotel uses a computer system to keep track of room bookings. the hotel staff are able to query a database to discover which rooms are booked or which rooms are free. (a) the hotel’s computer network uses a client-server model. (i) describe what is meant by the term ‘client-server’ in this context. [3] question answer mark guidance 1 (a) (i) 3 • client computers connect to server • server provides access to a resource/service ao1.2 • in this case hotel staff use client computers to connect to database on server (or other sensible example).","h44601-nov20-01-aii":"(a) the hotel’s computer network uses a client-server model. 1 a hotel uses a computer system to keep track of room bookings. the hotel staff are able to query a database to discover which rooms are booked or which rooms are free. (ii) give two advantages of client-server compared to peer-to-peer. 1 2 [2] the hotel’s network uses multiple switches. ii e.g. 2 • only one point of failure ao1.1 • easier to manage users/access • easier to backup • easier to keep data secure. • technicians can more easily remotely install / monitor.","h44601-nov20-01-b":"1 a hotel uses a computer system to keep track of room bookings. the hotel staff are able to query a database to discover which rooms are booked or whic