] position = position – 1 endwhile dataarray[position] = currentdata next x endprocedure","h44602-jun17-01-aii":"1 a programmer needs to sort an array of numeric data using an insertion sort. (ii) show how an insertion sort would sort the following data: 6 1 15 12 5 6 9 [6] 1 (a) (ii) 1 mark for contents of each row in table 6 … each row is dependent upon the ao2.1 preceding row being correct (6) 6 1 15 12 5 6 9 6 is the sorted list 1 1 6 15 12 5 6 9 1 is the compared to sorted list 1 is put in place in sorted list 15 is compared 1 1 6 15 12 5 6 9 15 is in place in sorted list 12 is compared 1 1 6 12 15 5 6 9 12 is in place in sorted list 5 is compared 1 1 5 6 12 15 6 9 5 is in place in sorted list 6 is compared 1 1 5 6 6 12 15 9 6 is in place in sorted list 12 15 9 is compared and put in place 1 1 5 6 6 9","h44602-jun17-01-bi":"1 a programmer needs to sort an array of numeric data using an insertion sort. (b) (i) using big-o notation state the best case complexity of insertion sort. [1] 1 (b) (i) o(n) 1 ao1.1 (1)","h44602-jun17-01-bii":"1 a programmer needs to sort an array of numeric data using an insertion sort. (ii) explain what your answer to part (b)(i) means. [3] 1 (b) (ii) 3 1 mark per bullet to max 3 b(ii) dependent upon b(i) being correct ao1.2 i.e. answers for o(n) only  the best case is for a sorted list (o(n)) (3) accept appropriate graph for bullet  as the number of elements increases points 2 and 3  … the number of steps increases in a linear fashion","h44602-jun17-01-c":"1 a programmer needs to sort an array of numeric data using an insertion sort. (c*) the number of data items in the array is continually increasing. insertion sort has a worst case time complexity of o(n2) and space complexity of o(1). an alternative sorting algorithm that could be used is bubble sort which also has a worst case time complexity of o(n2) and space complexity of o(1). briefly outline how the bubble sort algorithm works. discuss the relationship between the complexit